  "verbalization": "Amphetamine and Slc6a3 are linked through a shared pathway involving central nervous system stimulation. The evidence suggests that Amphetamine, as part of the broader class of central nervous system stimulants, binds to Slc6a3. This is supported by multiple paths that connect Amphetamine to Slc6a3 via Dextroamphetamine or Lisdexamfetamine, both of which are included in the Central Nervous System Stimulation category. The lowest common ancestors of these entities—Cns Stimulant and Amino Acid Amide—highlight a common functional role in the nervous system. The integration of these pathways implies that Amphetamine exerts its effects through a mechanism that ultimately involves Slc6a3, likely through a shared biological process. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Amphetamine and Slc6a3, mediated by the stimulant activity of Amphetamine, which is consistent across different compounds in the same class.",
